# %f, not %F: carrel's SECOND argument is a search PATTERN, not a second
# document — `carrel a.md b.md` searches a.md for the string "b.md" and exits
# without ever opening a reader. Handed a multi-file selection, %F made that
# the behaviour of double-clicking two documents in a file manager: a window
# that flashed and vanished. %f asks the launcher for one file per invocation,
# which is what a reader that opens one document at a time can honestly accept.
#
# There is deliberately no Icon= line. An icon name has to resolve to an entry
# in an installed icon theme, and no packaging recipe installs one, so
# `Icon=carrel` resolved to nothing wherever carrel is installed from a
# package. The desktop falls back to a generic icon either way, so the only
# thing the line added was a claim that is not true. Restore it in the same
# change that installs share/icons/hicolor/<size>/apps/carrel.png from all four
# recipes AND adds that file to dist-workspace.toml's `include` list —
# carrel-bin installs out of the release archive and can reach nothing the
# archive does not carry.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Carrel
GenericName=Markdown Reader
Comment=A quiet place to read your markdown
Exec=carrel %f
Terminal=true
Categories=Office;Viewer;
MimeType=text/markdown;text/x-markdown;
Keywords=markdown;reader;viewer;md;
